.TH ASTERCTL-SUBSCRIBE 1 "2026-09-28" "Aster" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
asterctl-subscribe \- create an Event subscription
.SH SYNOPSIS
.SY asterctl
.RI [ GLOBAL-OPTIONS ]
.B subscribe
.BI \-\-scope " SCOPE"
.BI \-\-operation\-key " KEY|auto"
.I TOPIC
.BI \-\-journal " PATH"
.BI \-\-client\-id " CLIENT_ID"
.YS
.SH DESCRIPTION
Create a persistent Event subscription for TOPIC. Subscriptions remain active
after the command exits and across agent restarts.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-scope " SCOPE"
Select the Event scope. Append '/*' to include sub-scopes.
.TP
.BI \-\-operation\-key " KEY|auto"
Use a UTF-8 key of 1\(en256 bytes, or
.B auto
to generate a new key.
.IP
For retries, use the actual key from the previous attempt and the same
subscription parameters.
.PP
Require the owning stable client ID and its retained durable journal. Explicit
recovery precedes mutation; a fenced incarnation cannot change subscriptions.
.SH OUTPUT
Prints the Base64 subscription ID to stdout.
.PP
With \-\-json, prints subscriptionId, inserted, and operation_key.
.PP
Generated operation keys are also printed to stderr before sending the request.
.PP
If the subscription already exists for that key and the same parameters,
the command succeeds and prints its ID to stdout. JSON reports inserted=false.
Reusing the key with different parameters still fails.
Earlier CLI versions returned status 1 for an identical existing subscription;
it now returns status 0, consistently with publication retries.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Subscription created or an identical existing subscription returned.
.TP
.B 1
Command failed.
.TP
.B 2
Invalid or missing arguments.
.SH EXAMPLES
Create a subscription with a generated key:
.PP
.nf
.RS
asterctl \-\-token\-file ./client.token subscribe \e
    \-\-journal ./publisher.redb \-\-client\-id chat-controller \e
    \-\-scope mission/team/alpha \e
    \-\-operation\-key auto \e
    chat.events
.RE
.fi
.PP
Use an explicit key and include sub-scopes:
.PP
.nf
.RS
asterctl \-\-token\-file ./client.token subscribe \e
    \-\-journal ./publisher.redb \-\-client\-id chat-controller \e
    \-\-scope 'mission/team/*' \e
    \-\-operation\-key chat-reader \e
    chat.events
.RE
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR asterctl (1),
.BR asterctl-query (1),
.BR asterctl-publish (1)
